## Security

Secrets must never appear in:

- Git
- source code
- configuration files committed to repository

Use environment variables or secret managers. See `ai-office/global/security-baseline.mdc`.

---

## Real-time / multiplayer requirements

When the task delivers a **networked / real-time** component (WebSocket game loop, matchmaking, live state sync):

- Validate every client message server-side (type, range, rate) before applying it to game state.
- Rate-limit or debounce client input to prevent flooding.
- Handle disconnect/reconnect explicitly (does the player's match/session survive a drop?).
- Keep game/simulation logic separate from transport/networking code.
- Log connect/disconnect, errors, and anomalous input patterns (possible cheating/abuse) where applicable.

Skip or narrow this section for **non-realtime** tasks (pure UI, docs-only, tooling) per Team Lead spec.

---

## Definition of Done

A task is complete when **acceptance criteria from the Team Lead's spec** are met. Typically this includes:

- Delivered artifacts match the task (code, configs, docs — as specified).
- **README** (or equivalent) updated if behaviour or setup changed.
- **README** and/or **`config.vars.example`** updated if new configuration surface was introduced.
- **No secrets** in the repository (`ai-office/global/security-baseline.mdc`).
- **Logging / observability** as required by the task.
- **Build / tests / run** — only what the spec requires.
- **Tester PASS** and, per the standard chain, a **Critic** verdict of `APPROVED` (or `ALL_CLOSED` from Judge after revision) — see `ai-office/process/review-judge-cycle.md`.
- **Player-facing mechanics docs (mandatory when applicable):** Shipping **player-facing mechanic changes or new player-facing features** must update `client/public/about.html` (and assets under `client/public/about/` as needed), bump the About page **Last updated** date, and add a **Changelog** entry (`client/public/changelog.json`) **in the same delivery / EPIC / PR** — not as a follow-up. See also `ai-office/policies/player-facing-docs.md`.

